  "parentPackage": "Regulation",
  "topLevelPackage": "GslEnterprise",
  "doc": "Baseline blood tests must be completed, resulted,\nand reviewed by a clinician before a hormone therapy\nprescription is authorised. The required baseline\npanel includes FBC, U&Es, LFTs, lipid profile,\nfasting glucose, prolactin, and baseline hormone\nlevels (testosterone, oestradiol).\n'Reviewed' means",
  "sourceFile": "exercises/gendersense/model/gsl-enterprise.sysml",
  "sourceDomain": "gsl",
  "metaModelLayer": "",
  "lineNumber": 107
 },
 {
  "kind": "requirement_def",
  "name": "ClinicalReviewBeforePrescribing",
  "parentPackage": "Regulation",
  "topLevelPackage": "GslEnterprise",
  "doc": "A clinician with appropriate competence must conduct\na clinical review before authorising a hormone therapy\nprescription. The review must consider baseline\ninvestigations, patient history, contraindications,\nand the proposed regimen.\nThis applies to both initial prescribing and any\nsubsequent dose a",
  "sourceFile": "exercises/gendersense/model/gsl-enterprise.sysml",
